==Battleground==
*Infinite [[Sir Seal]]s spawn after 3.33 seconds<sup>100f</sup>, delay 40~46.67 seconds<sup>1,200f~1,400f</sup>.
*5 [[Sir Seal]]s spawn after 40 seconds<sup>1,200f</sup>, delay 0.67~1.33 seconds<sup>20f~40f</sup>.
*3 [[Sir Seal]]s spawn after 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>, delay 0.67~1.33 seconds<sup>20f~40f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 90% HP:
**1 [[Camelle]] spawns as the boss.
**Infinite [[Sir Seal]]s spawn, delay 40~46.67 seconds<sup>1,200f~1,400f</sup>.
**Infinite [[Imperator Sael]]s spawn, delay 46.67~53.33 seconds<sup>1,400f~1,600f</sup>.
**Infinite [[Imperator Sael]]s spawn, delay 46.67~53.33 seconds<sup>1,400f~1,600f</sup>.
**Infinite [[Imperator Sael]]s spawn, delay 46.67~53.33 seconds<sup>1,400f~1,600f</sup>.

==Strategy==
Like most other stages in this sub-chapter, this stage is a joke if you have at least a few [[anti-unstarred Alien Treasures]]. Use [[Fish Cat (Normal Cat)|Island Cat]] or an otherwise better [[:Category:Anti-Red Cats|anti-Red]] Cat [[Crazed Fish Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Whale Cat]], [[Crazed Gross Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Sexy Legs Cat]] for extra wave DPS on Camelle and anything you have that can outrange Camelle, like [[Nerd Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Hacker Cat]]. You should never run out of money, as the Sir Seals provide plenty for the battle. Wave DPS from [[Crazed Gross Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Sexy Legs Cat]] and the Cat that can outrange Camelle should make this stage go pretty smoothly. It might take a while, but you could always use a [[Battle Items#Speed Up|Speed Up]].

